{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"code","value":"function injectRateLimitedSignal<TValue, TSelected>(\n   value,\n   initialOptions,\nselector?): RateLimitedSignal<TValue, TSelected>;","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Defined in: "},{"type":"link","href":"https://github.com/TanStack/pacer/blob/main/packages/angular-pacer/src/rate-limiter/injectRateLimitedSignal.ts#L58","children":[{"type":"text","value":"rate-limiter/injectRateLimitedSignal.ts:58"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"An Angular function that creates a rate-limited state signal, combining Angular's signal with rate limiting functionality.\nThis function provides both the current rate-limited value and methods to update it."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Rate limiting is a simple \"hard limit\" approach - it allows all updates until the limit is reached, then blocks\nsubsequent updates until the window resets. Unlike throttling or debouncing, it does not attempt to space out\nor intelligently collapse updates."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The function returns a callable object:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"rateLimited()"},{"type":"text","value":": Get the current rate-limited value"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"rateLimited.set(...)"},{"type":"text","value":": Set or update the rate-limited value (rate-limited via maybeExecute)"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"rateLimited.rateLimiter"},{"type":"text","value":": The rate limiter instance with additional control methods and state signals"}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"state-management-and-selector","children":[{"type":"text","value":"State Management and Selector"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The function uses TanStack Store for reactive state management via the underlying rate limiter instance.\nThe "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"selector"},{"type":"text","value":" parameter allows you to specify which rate limiter state changes will trigger signal updates,\noptimizing performance by preventing unnecessary subscriptions when irrelevant state changes occur."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"By default, there will be no reactive state subscriptions"}]},{"type":"text","value":" and you must opt-in to state\ntracking by providing a selector function. This prevents unnecessary updates and gives you\nfull control over when your component tracks state changes."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"type-parameters","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Type Parameters"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"tvalue","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TValue"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TValue"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"tselected","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TSelected"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TSelected"},{"type":"text","value":" = {\n}"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"parameters","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Parameters"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"value","children":[{"type":"text","value":"value"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TValue"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"initialoptions","children":[{"type":"text","value":"initialOptions"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"../type-aliases/AngularPacerOptions.md","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"AngularPacerOptions"}]},{"type":"text","value":"<"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"RateLimiterOptions"},{"type":"text","value":"<"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Setter"},{"type":"text","value":"<"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TValue"},{"type":"text","value":">>>"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"selector","children":[{"type":"text","value":"selector?"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"state"},{"type":"text","value":") => "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TSelected"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"returns","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"../interfaces/RateLimitedSignal.md","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"RateLimitedSignal"}]},{"type":"text","value":"<"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TValue"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TSelected"},{"type":"text","value":">"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"example","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Example"}]},{"type":"code","value":"// Default behavior - no reactive state subscriptions\nconst rateLimited = injectRateLimitedSignal(0, {\n  limit: 5,\n  window: 60000,\n  windowType: 'sliding'\n});\n\n// Opt-in to reactive updates when limit state changes\nconst rateLimited = injectRateLimitedSignal(\n  0,\n  { limit: 5, window: 60000 },\n  (state) => ({ rejectionCount: state.rejectionCount })\n);","lang":"ts"}],"headings":[{"id":"state-management-and-selector","text":"State Management and Selector","level":2},{"id":"type-parameters","text":"Type Parameters","level":2},{"id":"tvalue","text":"TValue","level":3},{"id":"tselected","text":"TSelected","level":3},{"id":"parameters","text":"Parameters","level":2},{"id":"value","text":"value","level":3},{"id":"initialoptions","text":"initialOptions","level":3},{"id":"selector","text":"selector?","level":3},{"id":"returns","text":"Returns","level":2},{"id":"example","text":"Example","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\n```ts\nfunction injectRateLimitedSignal<TValue, TSelected>(\n   value,\n   initialOptions,\nselector?): RateLimitedSignal<TValue, TSelected>;\n```\n\nDefined in: [rate-limiter/injectRateLimitedSignal.ts:58](https://github.com/TanStack/pacer/blob/main/packages/angular-pacer/src/rate-limiter/injectRateLimitedSignal.ts#L58)\n\nAn Angular function that creates a rate-limited state signal, combining Angular's signal with rate limiting functionality.\nThis function provides both the current rate-limited value and methods to update it.\n\nRate limiting is a simple \"hard limit\" approach - it allows all updates until the limit is reached, then blocks\nsubsequent updates until the window resets. Unlike throttling or debouncing, it does not attempt to space out\nor intelligently collapse updates.\n\nThe function returns a callable object:\n- `rateLimited()`: Get the current rate-limited value\n- `rateLimited.set(...)`: Set or update the rate-limited value (rate-limited via maybeExecute)\n- `rateLimited.rateLimiter`: The rate limiter instance with additional control methods and state signals\n\n## State Management and Selector\n\nThe function uses TanStack Store for reactive state management via the underlying rate limiter instance.\nThe `selector` parameter allows you to specify which rate limiter state changes will trigger signal updates,\noptimizing performance by preventing unnecessary subscriptions when irrelevant state changes occur.\n\n**By default, there will be no reactive state subscriptions** and you must opt-in to state\ntracking by providing a selector function. This prevents unnecessary updates and gives you\nfull control over when your component tracks state changes.\n\n## Type Parameters\n\n### TValue\n\n`TValue`\n\n### TSelected\n\n`TSelected` = \\{\n\\}\n\n## Parameters\n\n### value\n\n`TValue`\n\n### initialOptions\n\n[`AngularPacerOptions`](../type-aliases/AngularPacerOptions.md)\\<`RateLimiterOptions`\\<`Setter`\\<`TValue`\\>\\>\\>\n\n### selector?\n\n(`state`) => `TSelected`\n\n## Returns\n\n[`RateLimitedSignal`](../interfaces/RateLimitedSignal.md)\\<`TValue`, `TSelected`\\>\n\n## Example\n\n```ts\n// Default behavior - no reactive state subscriptions\nconst rateLimited = injectRateLimitedSignal(0, {\n  limit: 5,\n  window: 60000,\n  windowType: 'sliding'\n});\n\n// Opt-in to reactive updates when limit state changes\nconst rateLimited = injectRateLimitedSignal(\n  0,\n  { limit: 5, window: 60000 },\n  (state) => ({ rejectionCount: state.rejectionCount })\n);\n```\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: injectRateLimitedSignal\ntitle: injectRateLimitedSignal\n---\n\n```ts\nfunction injectRateLimitedSignal<TValue, TSelected>(\n   value,\n   initialOptions,\nselector?): RateLimitedSignal<TValue, TSelected>;\n```\n\nDefined in: [rate-limiter/injectRateLimitedSignal.ts:58](https://github.com/TanStack/pacer/blob/main/packages/angular-pacer/src/rate-limiter/injectRateLimitedSignal.ts#L58)\n\nAn Angular function that creates a rate-limited state signal, combining Angular's signal with rate limiting functionality.\nThis function provides both the current rate-limited value and methods to update it.\n\nRate limiting is a simple \"hard limit\" approach - it allows all updates until the limit is reached, then blocks\nsubsequent updates until the window resets. Unlike throttling or debouncing, it does not attempt to space out\nor intelligently collapse updates.\n\nThe function returns a callable object:\n- `rateLimited()`: Get the current rate-limited value\n- `rateLimited.set(...)`: Set or update the rate-limited value (rate-limited via maybeExecute)\n- `rateLimited.rateLimiter`: The rate limiter instance with additional control methods and state signals\n\n## State Management and Selector\n\nThe function uses TanStack Store for reactive state management via the underlying rate limiter instance.\nThe `selector` parameter allows you to specify which rate limiter state changes will trigger signal updates,\noptimizing performance by preventing unnecessary subscriptions when irrelevant state changes occur.\n\n**By default, there will be no reactive state subscriptions** and you must opt-in to state\ntracking by providing a selector function. This prevents unnecessary updates and gives you\nfull control over when your component tracks state changes.\n\n## Type Parameters\n\n### TValue\n\n`TValue`\n\n### TSelected\n\n`TSelected` = \\{\n\\}\n\n## Parameters\n\n### value\n\n`TValue`\n\n### initialOptions\n\n[`AngularPacerOptions`](../type-aliases/AngularPacerOptions.md)\\<`RateLimiterOptions`\\<`Setter`\\<`TValue`\\>\\>\\>\n\n### selector?\n\n(`state`) => `TSelected`\n\n## Returns\n\n[`RateLimitedSignal`](../interfaces/RateLimitedSignal.md)\\<`TValue`, `TSelected`\\>\n\n## Example\n\n```ts\n// Default behavior - no reactive state subscriptions\nconst rateLimited = injectRateLimitedSignal(0, {\n  limit: 5,\n  window: 60000,\n  windowType: 'sliding'\n});\n\n// Opt-in to reactive updates when limit state changes\nconst rateLimited = injectRateLimitedSignal(\n  0,\n  { limit: 5, window: 60000 },\n  (state) => ({ rejectionCount: state.rejectionCount })\n);\n```\n"}
